  "answer_text": "It looks like you may be referring to **Iuka, Mississippi** (sometimes misspelled as \"Luka\"). Here's an overview:\n\n### Iuka, Mississippi\n\n- **Iuka** (pronounced /a\u026a\u02c8ju\u02d0k\u0259/) is a city and the **county seat of Tishomingo County**, Mississippi, United States.\n\n- Its population was **3,139** at the 2020 census.\n\n- **Woodall Mountain**, the highest point in Mississippi, is located just south of Iuka.\n\n- Iuka is built on the site of a **Chickasaw village**, and the name \"Iuka\" comes from the name of one of the chiefs of that village.\n\n- Iuka was founded by **David Hubbard**, a wagon train scout, and Euro-American settlers arrived with the Memphis and Charleston Railroad in **1857**.\n\n- The Civil War brought widespread devastation when a major engagement \u2014 the **Battle of Iuka** \u2014 occurred on September 19, 1862, resulting in 1,200 to 1,500 killed or wounded.\n\n- Iuka is located in **northeast Mississippi**. U.S. Route 72 runs through the southern part of the city from west to east.\n\n- There are also **six artesian springs** in Iuka Springs Park, though currently only three are still flowing.\n\nIs there something more specific about Iuka (or \"Luka\"), Mississippi you'd like to know? \ud83d\ude0a",
